cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Tierra Viva: ESP32-P4 hardware stress test"
abstract: >-
  A real-world stress test of the ESP32-P4: both RISC-V cores at 86-96 % with the PPA, DMA, hardware JPEG and hardware crypto working at once, rendering a live Earth (sunlight, satellite clouds, earthquakes, ISS, ~6,500 aircraft) on a 2.8-inch touchscreen at 21-24 fps with no GPU, with internet over a USB tunnel or an ESP32-C3 running ESP-Hosted.
